'''bee-bread''' (bē′-bred), ''n.'' [Not found in ME.; AS. ''beó-breád'', ''bībreád'' = MHG. ''bie brōt'', G. ''bienen-brot'' = Sw. ''bibröt'', orig. (in AS.) the honey-comb with the honey, < ''beó'', bee, + ''breád'', bread.] '''1.''' A variously colored substance, the pollen of flowers, collected by bees as food for their young. See ''bee''<sup>1</sup>.—'''2.''' A plant much visited by bees or cultivated for their use, as red clover, ''Trifolium pratense'', or borage, ''Borago officinalis''.

